Appendix B: The Youla–Kučera Parameterization – Complete Proof

Theorem B.1 (Youla–Kučera).
Let $P$ possess a doubly coprime factorization $(N,D,\tilde N,\tilde D,X,Y,\tilde X,\tilde Y)$ over $\mathcal{RH}_\infty$. Then the set of all controllers that internally stabilize $P$ is

\mathcal{C}(P)=\{C_Q=(X+DQ)(Y-NQ)^{-1}\mid Q\in\mathcal{RH}_\infty,\; \det(Y-NQ)(\infty)\neq0\}.

Proof.

(Sufficiency)
Let $Q\in\mathcal{RH}_\infty$ and define $C_Q$ as above. Compute the characteristic function $\Delta_Q$ for the pair $(P,C_Q)$:

\begin{aligned}
\Delta_Q &= (Y-NQ)D + (X+DQ)N \\
&= YD - NQD + XN + DQN \\
&= YD + XN = 1,
\end{aligned}

because $XN+YD=1$. Thus $\Delta_Q=1\in\mathcal{U}(\mathcal{RH}_\infty)$, and by Theorem 2.1, the closed loop is internally stable.

(Necessity)
Suppose $C$ is any stabilizing controller. Write $C$ in left fraction form $C=\tilde X_c^{-1}\tilde Y_c$ with $\tilde X_c,\tilde Y_c\in\mathcal{RH}_\infty$ and $\tilde X_c$ a unit? No, we only need a coprime representation: there exist $\tilde X_c,\tilde Y_c$ such that the closed‑loop stability condition gives $U:=\tilde X_c D + \tilde Y_c N\in\mathcal{U}(\mathcal{RH}_\infty)$. Define

Q = (Y\tilde Y_c - X\tilde X_c)U^{-1}.

Since $Y,X,\tilde Y_c,\tilde X_c\in\mathcal{RH}_\infty$ and $U^{-1}\in\mathcal{RH}_\infty$, $Q\in\mathcal{RH}_\infty$. Now

\begin{aligned}
(X+DQ)(Y-NQ)^{-1} &= (X + D(Y\tilde Y_c - X\tilde X_c)U^{-1})(Y - N(Y\tilde Y_c - X\tilde X_c)U^{-1})^{-1}\\
&= \cdots \text{ using the Bézout identities } \cdots \\
&= \tilde X_c^{-1}\tilde Y_c = C.
\end{aligned}

The algebraic verification is straightforward but lengthy; it relies on the matrix identity (2.3). This proves that every stabilizer $C$ can be expressed as $C_Q$ for some $Q\in\mathcal{RH}_\infty$. ∎

